"answer": "The emails regarding Project Zenith outline its lifecycle and key developments. The project was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial phase one budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. Subsequently, the executive board approved a larger budget of $2 million to cover all research, development, and marketing phases. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture in September. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated in October. In November, Neil reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics for phase two. Strategic partnerships were established with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology, following earlier exploratory discussions. Finally, security protocols were updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective from January of the following year."
